expect \[zpwg8\] periph type=powergrid_voltage_gauge .*getValue=(11\.9\d*|12(\.0\d*)?)
expect \[zpwg8\] periph type=powergrid_current_gauge current=
expect \[zpwg8\] periph type=powergrid_redstone_converter
expect \[zpwg8\] conv override=7(\.0)?
expect \[zpwg8\] conv override=null
expect \[zpwg8\] dlink source pos=.*powergrid:voltage_gauge value=
expect \[zpwg8\] board create:display_board nbt=
reject \[zpwg8\] (periph|conv|dlink|board): no
reject \[zpwg8\] periph: none for
reject LuaException
reject \[zpwg\w*\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look periph maxRange / rangePercentage = 12 / range; current gauge current= the SQ-PWG-64 gauge value; converter terminal voltage in the be reads follows override 7 then clear (record both), and the be after the computer start shows the 7 override's voltage; shell 1: startup.lua present; shell 2 (computer file): start, three "sample N peripherals=2" blocks each with a powergrid_voltage_gauge line (voltage= about 12) and a powergrid_redstone_converter line, "<side> setValue(7) ok=true" and "<side> clearValue ok=true" (record the side names), end, no error text; dlink lines: activeTarget not none (none: the board is not its own controller yet, rerun dlink after a wait); board nbt text contains the gauge value with its unit (about 12 V, then about -5 V in polarized mode 2); no file: computer did not start (On:1b, computercraft/computer/7/), rerun by hand in CQ-PWG-21
